leds: flash: lm3601x: read the enable register from the chip

The chip returns to standby by itself at the flash timeout, but the
enable register was cached: flash_strobe kept reading 1 after the flash
had ended. Make it volatile.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/drivers/leds/flash/leds-lm3601x.c b/drivers/leds/flash/leds-lm3601x.c
index 62d65b554..e9f7871ed 100644
--- a/drivers/leds/flash/leds-lm3601x.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/flash/leds-lm3601x.c
@@ -111,6 +111,8 @@ static const struct reg_default lm3601x_regmap_defs[] = {
 static bool lm3601x_volatile_reg(struct device *dev, unsigned int reg)
 {
 	switch (reg) {
+	/* the chip clears the mode at the flash timeout */
+	case LM3601X_ENABLE_REG:
 	case LM3601X_FLAGS_REG:
 		return true;
 	default:
